# Object storage (Cloudflare R2 or MinIO)
# When unset, repair photos stay in Postgres.
#
# Cloudflare R2 (private bucket — recommended for repair photos):
# - Create a bucket with public access disabled.
# - Create an R2 API token scoped to that bucket (Object Read & Write).
# - Attachments upload via presigned PUT URLs or server-side Put; downloads use
#   authenticated API routes or presigned GET — nothing is world-readable.
# OBJECT_STORAGE_ENDPOINT=https://<ACCOUNT_ID>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# OBJECT_STORAGE_REGION=auto
# OBJECT_STORAGE_BUCKET=techlane-attachments
# OBJECT_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=<R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID>
# OBJECT_STORAGE_SECRET_KEY=<R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY>
# Optional CDN/public prefix (only if you deliberately expose objects elsewhere):
# OBJECT_STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE=
#
# Local MinIO (docker-compose):
# OBJECT_STORAGE_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
# OBJECT_STORAGE_REGION=auto
# OBJECT_STORAGE_BUCKET=techlane-attachments
# OBJECT_STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=techlane
# OBJECT_STORAGE_SECRET_KEY=techlanesecret
#
# Migrate existing Postgres BYTEA attachments after enabling storage:
#   go run ./cmd/migrate-attachments --dry-run
#   go run ./cmd/migrate-attachments
